[Music]  marvel never disappoints when it comes  to cameos and surprise reveals and the  latest could change thor's story forever  in fact the mid-credits scene and thor  love and thunder may have teased a major  battle warning spoilers ahead the thor  movies have always tried to find the  humanity in omnipotent gods thor odin's  son may be worshipped across the lands  but at the end of the day he's really  just looking for acceptance and love  from those he holds dear nowhere is that  more evident than in his latest  excursion thor love and thunder the  stories of tony stark and steve rogers  may have closed their final chapters but  thor's saga is still being written in  between battling aliens and getting into  verbal spars with the guardians of the  galaxy thor's really just looking for a  new purpose you see things didn't  exactly end well between him and his  former flame jane foster sorry to hear  that jane dumped you  she didn't dump me you know  i dumped her mutual dumping  when she comes back into his life things  get complicated quickly they'll work  together to bring down gore the god  butcher and in the process thor may just  realize that it's better to love those  close to you for the short time you'll  be together than to go through a mortal  life alone that said where one battle  ends another seems just to be beginning  throughout his latest adventure thor  gets into some trouble in omnipotent  city when he strikes down zoos at first  it seems like the greek god is dead but  as we see in the mid-credits scene he's  still very much among the living and he  has some substantial plans to get back  at thor by sending one of his own after  him it seems obvious that it would take  quite a bit more than a lightning bolt  through the chest to take down a god  especially one so adept at wielding his  own electrical powers and as the tag  reveals he's still around surrounded by  his mistresses the scene starts with  this tableau featuring zeus speaking to  someone else off screen and it's clear  he holds a mighty big grudge against the  god of thunder toward the end of his  speech zeus makes it clear that he wants  an unseen warrior to take thor down a  peg it's at this point that we finally  get a look at who's on the other side of  this conversation  it's revealed that hercules played by  ted lasso star brett goldstein is now in  the marvel cinematic universe he looks  determined to make his father proud it's  at this point the screen cuts to black  and the rest of the credits roll it  doesn't give away much but it does imply  that hercules will get into a  confrontation with thor down the road it  wouldn't be out of the question for this  to transpire in a possible thor 5  especially seeing how the very end of  the credits promises that thor will  return it seems as though his trip to  omnipotent city will have wide-ranging  consequences when it comes to getting on  the wrong side of the greek pantheon  naturally hercules in marvel comics is  based on the hero from greek mythology  with a few noteworthy twists he's been  around in the comics for a while through  various iterations but his formal  introduction to mass audiences came in  the 1960s when he was introduced as a  rival to thor from that point forward he  became a regular fixture in thor comics  occasionally being a thorn in thor's  side but also being an ally given his  introduction in thor love and thunder it  would make the most amount of sense for  him to follow a similar trajectory in  the mcu it's possible hercules will  initially function as a rival but the  two will likely become friends over time  and team up to fight a much larger  threat and from there the sky's the  limit with the character in the comics  hercules went on to join the avengers  that team may be in a state of flux at  the moment but it'll inevitably reunite  and hercules could certainly factor into  that equation hercules has a long  history from the comics to pull from so  it's unlikely this will be the last time  we see him on screen as a part of the  marvel cinematic universe check out one  of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about sore love  and thunder are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]

